WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.590
Channing Tatum, what were you thinking?

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:06.730
This look says:

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:12.150
“I am the Douchiest elf in all of Middle
Earth!”

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.170
Wait I have more disses for Channing Tatum!

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:16.360
He looks like Link from Twilight Princess,

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.529
if he OD'd on HGH!

00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:21.089
He looks like a level 63 Blood Elf

00:00:21.089 --> 00:00:23.060
who moonlights at Chippendales!

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.369
He looks like Peter Pan

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:26.849
with several extra “Y” chromosomes!

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:28.519
He looks like a version of Spock

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:30.169
from a parallel universe

00:00:30.169 --> 00:00:32.390
where everyone is FABULOUS!

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.590
He looks like a Yuuzhan Vong's

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.489
profile picture on GRINDR.

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:37.640
I assess the new movie Jupiter Ascending--

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.550
--on this week's episode of Angry Nerd!

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:42.460
First, your comments.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.090
I asked you what you thought of

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.630
the Jupiter Ascending trailer.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.019
The kindest comment

00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:48.030
was that it looked like

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.440
a ripoff of the indie RPG

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.149
Stars Without Number.

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:53.789
Most comments just bagged on Tatum's ears,

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:55.829
and his apparent use of eyeliner.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:57.170
Good call Buddy Smith,

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.379
he does look kinda like

00:00:58.379 --> 00:01:02.190
Mugatu in Zoolander!

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.559
The Wachowski's new movie

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:06.020
is a target-rich environment.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.020
For starters,

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.900
the protagonist is named Jupiter Jones.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.900
What, is she

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.080
a distant cousin of Pluto Nash?

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.330
But what really broils my bantha

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.040
is that the movie is about

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:21.320
a janitor whose genetic signature

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.550
proves that she's a descendant

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.410
of galactic rulers.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:29.290
I hate this strain of scifi stories

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.760
in which the characters are

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.830
fated to succeed.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:36.220
Now, predestination isn't a new storytelling
crutch;

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.330
but it's lazy!

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.250
It's positively feudal!

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.520
It's UNAMERICAN!

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.350
Heroism is about smarts

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.600
and adaptability,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.250
with maybe some bravery and self-sacrifice

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.260
thrown in there.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.890
But fate or kismet?

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:52.750
No thank you.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.430
This kind of thing reduces an epic saga

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:57.720
to a silly schoolboy's daydream

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.810
that he'd one day develop mutant powers,

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.470
and then he'd teach a lesson

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.750
to all of the bullies

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.800
who mocked his Jean-Luc Picard lunchbox,

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.179
and forced him to call home in tears and say,

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:14.780
“Mommy, I don't wanna go to college any
more!”.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.420
--which happened to a friend of mine!

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:17.920
Lana and Andy Wachoswksi,

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.829
you don't return my text messages
,

00:02:19.829 --> 00:02:20.989
but hear me out:

00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:21.989
While you're working on

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:23.930
your upcoming Netflix show Sens8,

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:26.530
try to make sure the characters

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.459
aren't already a lock to save the world

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:30.959
in the pilot episode.

00:02:30.959 --> 00:02:34.390
In fact, maybe do away with the characters
altogether

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.180
y’know, like you did

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.349
in Speed Racer.

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:41.920
Which movie hero do you think

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.239
had an unfair advantage over their foes?

00:02:44.239 --> 00:02:45.260
Let me know in the comments,

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.390
and subscribe to the WIRED channel!

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.459
ALSO, you are predestined

00:02:49.459 --> 00:02:51.040
to click on my other videos

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.349
that are over here to my left--

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:53.579
and your right!

00:02:53.579 --> 00:02:54.799
Like them!

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:56.750
Add comments to each of them!

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.579
Do it!

00:02:58.579 --> 00:03:00.909
Fulfill your galactic destiny!

